adjudication_explanation_Z:
**D5 (bias in selection of the reported result).** For Reviewer B's **Low** to hold, the route in Figure 7 / Table 14 needs 5.2 and 5.3 both N/PN, and then 5.1 Y/PY ("Trial analysed in accordance with a pre-specified plan?" → Y/PY → Low). The best case for Low runs like this:
- the registry entry was made before enrolment;
- the reported AE categories (liver, haematology, GI, skin/hypersensitivity) match the registered ones;
- the 30-day window plausibly reflects the 30-day high-dose period.

That case does not survive the guidance. Box 11 (5.1) asks whether the result was analysed under a plan "finalized before unblinded outcome data were available" and detailed enough to compare planned with reported measurements. The only such document is the registry outcome "Grade 3 and 4 and serious adverse events… Within 60 days". That is an outcome description, not an analysis plan. It also conflicts with the reported result in two ways:
- the window is 30 days, not 60 (article p. 3);
- the AE definition is "possibly/probably related" with neurological events and respiratory failure excluded (p. 10), which is not in the registry.

Neither change is explained. Box 11 lets such changes pass only if they were made before the data were available or were "clearly unrelated to the results". Neither can be shown here, so 5.1 cannot be Y/PY. For 5.2, Box 11 allows N/PN only with "clear evidence… that all eligible reported results… correspond to all intended outcome measurements" or where "trialists have provided the reason for the inconsistency". Neither condition is met, so 5.2 is NI rather than PN. With 5.2 = NI, Table 14 (row "Any answer | NI | N/PN") gives Some concerns, whatever the answer to 5.1.

I also checked whether my own Some concerns should go up to High. That needs 5.2 or 5.3 to be Y/PY, which per Box 11 needs clear evidence that the result was "likely to have been selected on the basis of the results". There is none:
- the reported counts add up (12+1+1+1 = 15);
- the result is null;
- the analysis is a single descriptive proportion, so 5.3 = PN.

So High is not supported either. Reviewers A and C both give the defensible judgement, Some concerns, and I pick A only as the first of the two identical answers. Agreement between A and C was not the reason. My answers to the signalling questions are unchanged.

CHOICE: D5=A
REVISED: D5=Some concerns
